NEARS-2816 QA — AC1 live reproduction, emulator-5556, worktree build (com.izzes.nears / com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_2816_cart_merge_banner)

Backend confirms cart_merged:false was genuinely computed and returned on the login response
(Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log):
[2026-09-02 13:52:55] production.WARNING: [FAIL] guest.cart.merge.rejected {"trace_id":"c5c1ebf2530803cb566d167b94742352","correlation_id":"0a2a3812-9ed2-4f64-9346-ade18561ccd0","reason":"token_mismatch","guest_id":"1401","request_id":"0a2a3812-9ed2-4f64-9346-ade18561ccd0"}

Repro mechanism: a real guest cart was created for guest_id=1401 via the app's own UI (Add To
Cart as guest, matched real guest_token in secure storage). A surgical reverse proxy
(127.0.0.1:8010 -> 127.0.0.1:8000) corrupted ONLY the guest_token field of the app's own
POST /api/v1/auth/login request body (JSON) to a bogus value, leaving every other guest-scoped
call (cart/add, cart/list, guest/request) untouched with the real token -- so no unrelated 401
fired and no self-heal guest-session re-mint occurred before the login attempt (see
lib/api/api_checker.dart's global 401 force-logout+re-mint, which DOES fire on any OTHER guest
401 and silently wipes/replaces guest_id+guest_token, defeating a naive "edit local
SharedPreferences guest_id" repro -- confirmed live, guest_id incremented 1392->1397 across
relaunches purely from boot-time guest calls tripping that handler).

CLIENT SIDE — the pending flag IS correctly armed by this login response:
  before login:  key flutter.6ammart_cart_merge_banner_pending ABSENT
  after login:   flutter.6ammart_cart_merge_banner_pending = true   (auth_service.dart's
                 `authResponse.cartMerged == false` branch fired correctly)

CLIENT SIDE — on the NEXT fresh HomeScreen mount (force-stop + relaunch, landing directly on
Home since address/module were already saved), the flag IS consumed:
  after relaunch: key flutter.6ammart_cart_merge_banner_pending ABSENT (removed)
  -> maybeShowCartMergeBanner() ran, pending==true, NSnackBar.show(...) WAS called.

YET the banner text ("We couldn't restore your saved cart items, please re-add them") NEVER
appeared on screen. Instrument: 10x `adb shell uiautomator dump` at ~0.8s spacing, spanning the
full splash->Home mount window (logcat: "route: initial route module=null" at 13:54:18.800,
i.e. HomeScreen's first build, well inside the poll window 13:54:17.x-13:54:25.x) -- zero
matches for "restore your saved cart items" in any of the 10 dumps. No FlutterError, no
exception, no red screen (`ui_errors` clean apart from an unrelated pre-existing
GetPositionFailure). Positive control: the SAME dumps DO contain real, unrelated content-desc
nodes ("House: 10 Av 2, Dhaka 1216, Bangladesh", "Grocery & Food, 6 stores near you", etc.),
proving the accessibility instrument was live and not silently empty (see the paired
bug-ac1-banner-not-rendered-dump.xml, one representative dump, dump #5 of 10).

Reproduced independently 3 times across this session, in 3 different scenarios:
  1. customer@nears.com, zone 1, WITH a competing "payment was Incomplete" NBottomSheet
     (Get.context-rooted modal from DashboardScreen.initState) shown on the same first Home
     frame -- banner never appeared across 12x 1s-spaced dumps while the modal sat open.
  2. qa.cartbanner2816@nears.com (fresh signup, 0 orders, no competing dialog), login
     triggered from the Profile tab -> returns to ProfileScreen in place (does NOT navigate to
     Home) -- HomeScreen was never (re)mounted by the login itself; the flag sat pending,
     unconsumed, until the NEXT genuine Home visit/app restart.
  3. Same account, clean fresh app launch (zero competing dialogs, zero orders, first-ever
     HomeScreen mount this install) -- flag correctly consumed on this exact mount, yet the
     banner still never appeared in 10x 0.8s-spaced dumps. This is the cleanest possible case
     and still fails -- the defect is not solely the modal-collision or the ProfileScreen-return
     navigation path; NSnackBar.show(...) itself does not appear to make the toast visible from
     this call site.

Automated widget tests (cart_merge_banner_test.dart) pump maybeShowCartMergeBanner() against a
minimal MaterialApp+Scaffold+mocked AuthRepositoryInterface and DO find the SnackBar text via
find.text() -- consistent with a real widget-tree/context mismatch specific to the live
Dashboard/HomeScreen composition, not a broken NSnackBar/NToast widget in isolation.
